--------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Why AGPL-3.0-or-later
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The app ships Strudel and superdough, both AGPL-3.0-or-later, to every player
over the network. Section 13 of the AGPL obliges whoever runs a modified
version for users over a network to offer those users the corresponding
source. This repository is that offer. The app's "Source & Credits" link (on
the loading screen) points at the tree of the deployed commit; builds that do
not know their commit fall back to the main branch.

The licence applies to the repository as a whole. Content that is not code
(fonts, sample audio, song transcriptions) is a separate question and is
covered below, not by LICENSE.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Strudel and superdough (AGPL-3.0-or-later)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Runtime dependencies, all by the Strudel / TidalCycles community (Alex McLean,
Felix Roos and contributors), https://strudel.cc, https://codeberg.org/uzu/strudel:

  @strudel/codemirror 1.3.0   @strudel/core 1.2.6       @strudel/mini 1.2.6
  @strudel/soundfonts 1.3.0   @strudel/tonal 1.2.6      @strudel/transpiler 1.2.6
  @strudel/webaudio 1.3.0     superdough 1.3.0

The app ships a patched superdough 1.3.0 and a patched @strudel/soundfonts
1.3.0 (and a patched @codemirror/view 6.40.0, which is MIT). The patches are in
this repository under patches/ and are applied at install time through the
"patchedDependencies" field in package.json. Together with the unmodified
upstream package versions named above, they are the corresponding source of
what is served. The superdough patch is a diff of the published dist build, not
of the upstream source tree.

The app is moving to its own audio engine (src/audio/live/). Once no Strudel
code ships, this section and the licence choice are due for review. Published
snapshots stay AGPL either way.

