--------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Hilbert scope
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Hilbert scope renderer was influenced by Seeing Music (Creatability,
Google Creative Lab) and adapts the Hamming-window impulse, convolution filter
and compensating delay of its Web Audio adapter, which in turn credits
conundrumer/Audioscope. Both upstream licences are GNU GPL version 3, which
combines with AGPL-3.0. Sources, authors and links are in docs/credits.md.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. Sample packs and soundfonts loaded at runtime
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

These are fetched by the player's browser; they are not in this repository.

  felixroos/dough-samples (raw.githubusercontent.com)
    The repository itself declares no licence; each pack is documented in its
    README. The app loads two packs:
    - piano: Salamander Grand Piano V3, by Alexander Holm,
      CC BY 3.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/).
      Attribution required: https://archive.org/details/SalamanderGrandPianoV3
    - vcsl: Versilian Community Sample Library, CC0
      (https://github.com/sgossner/VCSL).

  General MIDI soundfonts (felixroos.github.io/webaudiofontdata, via
  @strudel/soundfonts)
    The webaudiofontdata repository is MIT. It converts several soundfonts;
    by count in @strudel/soundfonts' General MIDI map, GeneralUserGS (most
    instruments), Aspirin, JCLive, Chaos, LesPaul, Stratocaster and SBAWE32.
    Its README links the GeneralUserGS and FluidR3 licences. The individual
    terms of GeneralUserGS, Aspirin, JCLive, Chaos, LesPaul, Stratocaster
    and SBAWE32 are unverified here.

